hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23613","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us from Ismail ibn Umayyah from a freedman of theirs from Muzahim ibn Abi Muzahim from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah ibn Khalid ibn Asid from a man from Khuza'ah called Mihrash or Mukharrish, Sufyan would not settle upon his name, and perhaps he said: Mikhrash, and I did not hear it myself, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out from al-Ji'ranah by night, then performed Umrah, then returned and morninged there as one who had spent the night; I looked at his back as if it were an ingot of silver."
